{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_13-51-31-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\n \\\"rationale\\\": (\\\"Registers the third sourced lead (a completion endpoint that can report success for an entry that was never decided at the reported index) and requests the probe that \\\"\n  \\\"constructs it; no execution result is claimed yet.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_superseded_doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/event.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":126,\\\"end_line\\\":137,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_decided_sub_push\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":296,\\\"end_line\\\":333,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@q_overwritten_index\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\": (\\\"Can append_notify resolve Ok(idx) for an entry that was never decided at idx - specifically when the index the call was assigned is later occupied by a different entry - and \\\"\n    \\\"is the documented Superseded heuristic therefore shadowed by the index-only check?\\\"),\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_drain_notifiers_timeout\\\",\\\"src_append_notify_contract\\\",\\\"src_superseded_doc\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\": (\\\"drain_notifiers matches on the pending item's assignment in the order \"'`Some((idx, _)) if idx <= decided` first and `Some((idx, ballot)) if ballot < cur_ballot` second, so once the \"\n    \"node'\"'s decided index covers the assigned index the call resolves Ok(idx) even if leadership moved on and the entry was overwritten; the Ok contract (await its decided log index, and the \\\"\n    \\\"documented usage 'durably decided at log idx') is then false, and the Superseded heuristic that was written for exactly this leadership-change case never fires.\\\"),\n   \\\"discriminator\\\": (\\\"Construction that isolates the assigned index from its entry: node A is the leader and accepts its own entry at index 1 with its outgoing and incoming traffic cut, so the entry \\\"\n    \\\"never leaves A; nodes B and C then elect B and decide index 1 with B's own entry; A is let back in and re-syncs, truncating its log to B's and raising its decided index to 1. If A's pending call \\\"\n    \\\"resolves Ok(1) while the entry at index 1 on A is B's entry and not A's, the index-only check is a false completion; if it resolves Superseded instead, the hypothesis is refuted.\\\"),\n   \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@q_overwritten_index\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"identity_probe.rs\\\",\n  \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\"omnipaxos_runtime\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_drain_notifiers_timeout\\\",\\\"src_append_notify_contract\\\",\\\"src_superseded_doc\\\",\\\"src_detect_events\\\",\\\"src_run_loop\\\"],\n  \\\"prefix\\\": (\\\"Three real OmniPaxos instances (pid 1,2,3) over MemoryStorage, each driven by a real omnipaxos_runtime actor from spawn_actor with a harness-local tokio-backed AsyncRuntime impl. \\\"\n   \\\"The transport is explicit: a pump task per node moves outgoing messages into a shared queue and a delivery task pops them and calls the receiver's handle_incoming, dropping messages whose \\\"\n   \\\"sender or receiver is currently isolated (\"'`blocked`/`blocked_in`). Node 1 has leader_priority 10 and becomes the leader after the initial heartbeats. Sequence: node 1 is first isolated in both \"\n   \"directions; `node1.append_notify(TestEntry(42))` is then accepted locally at index 1 (its own entry, read back as Undecided) and never leaves the node; `node2.try_become_leader()` makes node 2 \"\n   \"the leader with node 3'\"'s promise (its log is empty, since node 1's entry never left), and \"'`node2.append_notify(TestEntry(99))` is decided at index 1 by node 2 and node 3; node 1 is then \"\n   \"un-isolated and asked to reconnect to node 2, which makes it promise node 2, receive an AcceptSync that truncates its log to node 2'\"'s and raises its decided index to 1. The case emits CA_EVENT \\\"\n   \\\"after_b_takeover {b_leader,c_leader,a_leader,b_decided,c_decided} and CA_EVENT overwritten_index_resolution {a_decided_idx,a_entry_at_index_1_is_own,b_decided_idx,b_idx,resolution}, and asserts \\\"\n   \\\"that the resolved call reports Ok(idx) while the entry at that index on node 1 is not the entry that call submitted (and that node 2's own entry was assigned a different index). RuntimeConfig: \\\"\n   \\\"tick_period 2000ms (so the resolution tick cannot land between node 1's promise change and the sync), egress_period 1ms, append_notify_timeout 5s.\\\"),\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":(\\\"Focused construction of one completion-endpoint identity case: an assigned index that is decided while the entry originally assigned to it was overwritten.\\\"),\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"3 nodes, majority quorum; in-process delivery under harness control\\\",\\\"node 1's traffic is isolated in both directions while node 2 takes over, so node 1's entry cannot be adopted\\\",\\\"node 1 is re-admitted through a Promise + AcceptSync cycle, which is the protocol's normal re-synchronization path\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the default 1024 event capacity (unrelated here)\\\",\\\"any claim about how often this interleaving occurs in a deployment\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":3,\\\"tick_period_ms\\\":2000,\\\"append_notify_timeout_ms\\\":5000}},\n }\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_cod