s then \"\n   \"un-isolated and asked to reconnect to node 2, which makes it promise node 2, receive an AcceptSync that truncates its log to node 2'\"'s and raises its decided index to 1. The case emits CA_EVENT \\\"\n   \\\"after_b_takeover {b_leader,c_leader,a_leader,b_decided,c_decided} and CA_EVENT overwritten_index_resolution {a_decided_idx,a_entry_at_index_1_is_own,b_decided_idx,b_idx,resolution}, and asserts \\\"\n   \\\"that the resolved call reports Ok(idx) while the entry at that index on node 1 is not the entry that call submitted (and that node 2's own entry was assigned a different index). RuntimeConfig: \\\"\n   \\\"tick_period 2000ms (so the resolution tick cannot land between node 1's promise change and the sync), egress_period 1ms, append_notify_timeout 5s.\\\"),\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":(\\\"Focused construction of one completion-endpoint identity case: an assigned index that is decided while the entry originally assigned to it was overwritten.\\\"),\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"3 nodes, majority quorum; in-process delivery under harness control\\\",\\\"node 1's traffic is isolated in both directions while node 2 takes over, so node 1's entry cannot be adopted\\\",\\\"node 1 is re-admitted through a Promise + AcceptSync cycle, which is the protocol's normal re-synchronization path\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the default 1024 event capacity (unrelated here)\\\",\\\"any claim about how often this interleaving occurs in a deployment\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":3,\\\"tick_period_ms\\\":2000,\\\"append_notify_timeout_ms\\\":5000}},\n }\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"written\n